      "text": "83,732.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **692** and **121**, follow these easy steps:\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication:**\n\n   \\[\n   692 \\times 121 = 692 \\times (100 + 20 + 1)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 692 by each part separately:**\n\n   - **Multiply by 100:**\n     \\[\n     692 \\times 100 = 69,\\!200\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Multiply by 20:**\n     \\[\n     692 \\times 20 = 13,\\!840\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Multiply by 1:**\n     \\[\n     692 \\times 1 = 692\n     \\]\n\n3. **Add all the results together:**\n\n   \\[\n   69,\\!200 + 13,\\!840 + 692 = 83,\\!732\n   \\]\n\n4. **Final Answer:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{83,\\!732}\n   \\]",
