      "text": "348,605.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **405** and **861**, we'll perform the multiplication step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Multiplication\nWe can use the distributive property to simplify the multiplication:\n\n\\[\n405 \\times 861 = 405 \\times (800 + 60 + 1)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part\n1. **Multiply by 800:**\n   \\[\n   405 \\times 800 = 405 \\times 8 \\times 100 = 3,240 \\times 100 = 324,000\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply by 60:**\n   \\[\n   405 \\times 60 = 405 \\times 6 \\times 10 = 2,430 \\times 10 = 24,300\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Multiply by 1:**\n   \\[\n   405 \\times 1 = 405\n   \\]\n\n### Step 3: Add All the Results Together\n\\[\n324,000 + 24,300 + 405 = 348,705\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{348,\\!705}\n\\]",
