  "choices": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "303,140.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **710** and **427**, follow these easy steps:\n\n1. **Break Down the Multiplication:**\n\n   \\[\n   710 \\times 427 = 710 \\times (400 + 20 + 7)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply Each Part Separately:**\n\n   - **Multiply by 400:**\n     \\[\n     710 \\times 400 = 284,\\!000\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Multiply by 20:**\n     \\[\n     710 \\times 20 = 14,\\!200\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Multiply by 7:**\n     \\[\n     710 \\times 7 = 4,\\!970\n     \\]\n\n3. **Add All the Results Together:**\n\n   \\[\n   284,\\!000 + 14,\\!200 + 4,\\!970 = 303,\\!170\n   \\]\n\n4. **Final Answer:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{303,\\!170}\n   \\]",
      "logprobs": null,
