      "text": "146,115.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **255** and **573**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nUse the distributive property to simplify the multiplication:\n\\[\n255 \\times 573 = 255 \\times (500 + 70 + 3)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part\n1. **Multiply by 500:**\n\\[\n255 \\times 500 = 127,\\!500\n\\]\n2. **Multiply by 70:**\n\\[\n255 \\times 70 = 17,\\!850\n\\]\n3. **Multiply by 3:**\n\\[\n255 \\times 3 = 765\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Add All the Results Together\n\\[\n127,\\!500 + 17,\\!850 + 765 = 146,\\!115\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{146115}\n\\]",
