      "index": 0,
      "text": "118,296.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **318** and **372**, we'll perform the multiplication step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nWe can break down the multiplication to make it easier:\n\n\\[\n318 \\times 372 = (300 + 18) \\times (300 + 72)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Use the Distributive Property\nApply the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials):\n\n\\[\n(300 + 18) \\times (300 + 72) = 300 \\times 300 + 300 \\times 72 + 18 \\times 300 + 18 \\times 72\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate Each Part\n\n1. **\\(300 \\times 300\\):**\n   \\[\n   300 \\times 300 = 90,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n2. **\\(300 \\times 72\\):**\n   \\[\n   300 \\times 72 = 21,\\!600\n   \\]\n\n3. **\\(18 \\times 300\\):**\n   \\[\n   18 \\times 300 = 5,\\!400\n   \\]\n\n4. **\\(18 \\times 72\\):**\n   \\[\n   18 \\times 72 = 1,\\!296\n   \\]\n\n### Step 4: Add All the Parts Together\n\n\\[\n90,\\!000 + 21,\\!600 + 5,\\!400 + 1,\\!296 = 118,\\!296\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{118,\\!296}\n\\]",
