      "text": "296,625.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **375** and **775**, we'll perform the multiplication step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nWe can break down the multiplication into more manageable parts using the distributive property.\n\n\\[\n375 \\times 775 = (300 + 70 + 5) \\times (700 + 70 + 5)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part\nLet's multiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n300 \\times 700 &= 210,\\!000 \\\\\n300 \\times 70 &= 21,\\!000 \\\\\n300 \\times 5 &= 1,\\!500 \\\\\n70 \\times 700 &= 49,\\!000 \\\\\n70 \\times 70 &= 4,\\!900 \\\\\n70 \\times 5 &= 350 \\\\\n5 \\times 700 &= 3,\\!500 \\\\\n5 \\times 70 &= 350 \\\\\n5 \\times 5 &= 25 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Add All the Products Together\nNow, sum all the results from the previous step.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n210,\\!000 &+ 21,\\!000 + 1,\\!500 + 49,\\!000 + 4,\\!900 + 350 + 3,\\!500 + 350 + 25 \\\\\n&= 210,\\!000 + 21,\\!000 = 231,\\!000 \\\\\n231,\\!000 + 1,\\!500 &= 232,\\!500 \\\\\n232,\\!500 + 49,\\!000 &= 281,\\!500 \\\\\n281,\\!500 + 4,\\!900 &= 286,\\!400 \\\\\n286,\\!400 + 350 &= 286,\\!750 \\\\\n286,\\!750 + 3,\\!500 &= 290,\\!250 \\\\\n290,\\!250 + 350 &= 290,\\!600 \\\\\n290,\\!600 + 25 &= 290,\\!625 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{290,\\!625}\n\\]",
