      "text": "499,200.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **832** and **600**, follow these easy steps:\n\n1. **Break Down the Multiplication:**\n\n   \\[\n   832 \\times 600 = 832 \\times (6 \\times 100)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 832 by 6:**\n\n   \\[\n   832 \\times 6 = 4,\\!992\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply the Result by 100:**\n\n   \\[\n   4,\\!992 \\times 100 = 499,\\!200\n   \\]\n\n4. **Final Answer:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{499,\\!200}\n   \\]",
