      "text": "121,195.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **129** and **955**, we'll perform the multiplication step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Multiplication\nWe can use the distributive property to simplify the multiplication:\n\n\\[\n129 \\times 955 = 129 \\times (900 + 50 + 5)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part\n1. **Multiply by 900:**\n   \\[\n   129 \\times 900 = 116,\\!100\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply by 50:**\n   \\[\n   129 \\times 50 = 6,\\!450\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Multiply by 5:**\n   \\[\n   129 \\times 5 = 645\n   \\]\n\n### Step 3: Add All the Results Together\n\\[\n116,\\!100 + 6,\\!450 + 645 = 121,\\!195\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{121,\\!195}\n\\]",
